# Smoke test: login -> me -> S-01 (repository + version pattern) -> logout -> me (401).
# Run the API first: dotnet run --project api --launch-profile http
#
# Fill @userName and @password locally before running and never commit them.
# userName is the bare sAMAccountName (no DOMAIN\ prefix, no @suffix).
#
# The session is the sc_auth cookie (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict); the requests
# below rely on the client's cookie jar to resend it. Some REST clients do not resend a
# Secure cookie over plain http - if "me" returns 401 right after a successful login,
# run the https profile and set @host = https://localhost:7009.
#
# S-01 (requests 3-9) needs the database migrated and Git:* user-secrets set (see AGENTS.md).
# Fill @repoUrl with an https URL on a host listed in Git:AllowedHosts and @pattern with a
# pattern like 2.1.* that matches tags in that repository; never commit real values.
# The repository URL must not be registered yet (otherwise step 3 returns 409).
# Steps 4-9 read the IDs from the responses of the named requests addRepo and addPattern
# (Visual Studio, Rider and VS Code REST Client support this syntax).

@host = http://localhost:5143
@userName =
@password =
@repoUrl =
@pattern =

### 1. Login - expect 200 with { userName, displayName } and a Set-Cookie: sc_auth
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "{{userName}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2. Current user - expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/me
Accept: application/json

### 3. Add repository - expect 201 with the canonical URL (https://<host>/<path>.git, lower case)
# @name addRepo
POST {{host}}/api/repos
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "{{repoUrl}}"
}

### 4. Add version pattern - expect 201 with lastResolution.state Resolved and the tag
# @name addPattern
POST {{host}}/api/repos/{{addRepo.response.body.$.id}}/patterns
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pattern": "{{pattern}}"
}

### 5. Resolve again - expect 200 with the current tag and commit
POST {{host}}/api/patterns/{{addPattern.response.body.$.id}}/resolve

### 6. Deactivate - expect 200 with isActive false
POST {{host}}/api/patterns/{{addPattern.response.body.$.id}}/deactivate

### 7. Resolve an inactive pattern - expect 409
POST {{host}}/api/patterns/{{addPattern.response.body.$.id}}/resolve

### 8. Activate - expect 200 with isActive true
POST {{host}}/api/patterns/{{addPattern.response.body.$.id}}/activate

### 9. Change log - expect 200, newest first: PatternActivated, PatternDeactivated, PatternAdded, RepositoryAdded
GET {{host}}/api/repos/{{addRepo.response.body.$.id}}/events
Accept: application/json

### 10. Logout - expect 204 and the cookie cleared
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout

### 11. Current user after logout - expect 401
GET {{host}}/api/me
Accept: application/json
